# The sm_120 patch stack for SGLang, sha256-pinned.
#
# Source: github.com/gabrielolympie/sglang-flashnext-sm120 at commit
#         67d2f9234fa45ae1339f0d53cd37cb695e9c6493 (2026-08-31), which in turn
#         ports the sm_120 RecoverSSM/WY and fp8-QSA groundwork from
#         github.com/jpezzulli/sglang-rtxpro6000.
#
# fetch-patches.sh downloads these seven files into ./patches/ and verifies
# them against this list. They are fetched rather than vendored because the
# upstream repository carries no licence, so there is no redistribution grant.
#
# The six .patch files are diffs against sgl-project/sglang as of
# 2026-08-30/31; hot_tokens_64k.pt is the 64K FR-Spec draft-vocabulary map.
# These hashes were verified byte-for-byte against the deployment described in
# models/qwen3.8-flash-next.md.
#
# If you re-pin to a newer upstream commit, refresh every line here and re-read
# the patch-application notes on that page: which patches apply strictly and
# which need fuzz depends on the SGLang image you pin alongside them.

d1c8f7ea4450600da4963d128159f768b7b2bad89ff13cbc947a97bca202d2ff  0001b-recoverssm-wy-sm120-PORTED.patch
a85100107a0778acfa0457a0234c9aae730ab9ca2aace8bafc6074f81588237a  0002-fp8-qsa-tile-dequant.patch
71c61bde4d6c408bb941a8b9af2728c74c7f39697eefb76b1e19d72992f2b3f7  0003-sm120-fp32-prefill-state.patch
fb41905a2ca47dc357226cfecbe350116b42dffd25a14dafb67be0d84e64202f  0004-sm120-lowm-triton-gemm.patch
43de44f1266549118c1136b6c1fefc1e3b42d1da87347987ae08a29d621ca25b  0005-sm120-fp8-weight-only.patch
0cafb084741e828f5571acbf053365724004c6b4433f18a9f9e62a1c13209f0e  0006-sm120-fp8-hc-lmhead.patch
f03551e4709e50e5842b24912845c243bfe628b74bf185617fae7ebaaa0da86c  hot_tokens_64k.pt
